# CambiOS code ownership.
#
# Everything is owned unless a line below says otherwise. An owned path
# needs a code-owner review before a pull request that touches it can
# merge (branch protection: require_code_owner_reviews). The project's
# agent identity (cambios-agent) is not an owner, so it cannot merge a
# change to an owned path on its own.
#
# The earlier form of this file listed the owned paths and left the rest
# open. A directory created after the list was written was therefore
# unowned: the proof crates, the boot manifest, the trusted public key,
# every Cargo.lock, the hooks, and any new top-level crate. Ownership by
# default means a new path is reviewed until someone decides it need
# not be.
#
# In this file the last matching pattern wins, and a pattern with no
# owner makes the path unowned.

*                                 @riccajason

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hands-off lanes: unowned on purpose. A pull request touching only
# these merges on green checks, without an owner's review.
#
# The trade for each is stated, so it can be revisited.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# User-space crates. Looser rules than the kernel, and the place most
# outside work lands. `make check-user` and `make test-user` are what
# make a green check on this lane mean something.
/user/

# The status index and the bounds catalogue: updated with almost every
# change, by whoever made it. STATUS.md is at the repository root.
/STATUS.md
/docs/ASSUMPTIONS.md

# Generated documents (a lint fails when one is out of step with its
# source) and working notes.
/docs/generated/
/docs/dev-notes/

# Narrative and reference documents that carry no decision.
/docs/manuals/
/docs/developer-experience.md
/docs/storage-planning.md
/docs/identity-synthesis.md
/docs/INTERRUPT_ROUTING.md
/docs/SYSCALLS.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Owned inside a hands-off lane.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The system library is the user-space half of the syscall ABI.
/user/libsys/                     @riccajason

# A lockfile change is a dependency change, wherever the lockfile is.
Cargo.lock                        @riccajason
